   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "This is why grep finds the definition and the debugger does not. A macro has no\ntype, no scope and no address, so it can do things a function cannot, including\nevaluating its argument twice.",
   "originalText": "This is why grep finds the definition and the debugger does not. A macro has no\ntype, no scope and no address, so it can do things a function cannot, including\nevaluating its argument twice.",
